    "recommendations": "• Remove woody debris piles visible near structures before fire season.\n• Thin the tree cluster closest to the structure to increase open space between tree canopy and the building.\n• Cut grass around structures and outbuildings short, particularly during dry months.\n• Trim low-hanging branches on scattered trees near the house to reduce the path fire can travel from the ground upward.\n• Clear shrubs growing directly adjacent to or touching any structure.\n• Keep the single access route free of overhanging branches and encroaching vegetation so vehicles can pass through without obstruction.\n• Remove dead or dry woody material that has collected along the rear of the property where access is limited.\n• Thin shrubs in the rear yard area to allow better movement around the back of the structure.\n• Keep the open green space areas mowed and free of accumulated dead grass or plant debris.\n• Separate any remaining shrub groupings near structures so fire cannot move continuously from one shrub to the next toward the building."
